                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            at that point.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Dually
            in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras"} function algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+spectra"} formal spectra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
            algebras. The formal spectra of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+series"} Laurent series
            algebras are instead the “punctured formal disks”, hence formal disks with their unique global point removed.
          %p
            More concretely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-cohesive+site"} infinity-cohesive site
            of “differentiable spaces” (such as for instance
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+manifolds"} complex analytic manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi synthdiff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{synthdiff}
            is the corresponding site of infinitesimal thickenings (for instance complex analytic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+loci"} smooth loci
            of the form the product of a complex manifold with an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+point"} infinitesimally thickened point
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi synthdiff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(S_{synthdiff})
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi InfPoints
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(InfPoints)
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} synthetic differential ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            takes it to its union
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat X
